+EIGHTMAX TEST WORKBENCH 0.36.2 - MILESTONE 2 WINDOWS TESTS (simulator window lifecycle)
+=====================================================================================
+
+What this tests on YOUR computer, with real windows:
+  - a simulator window that closes is detected and NOT captured again (no repeated target-lost)
+  - queued / running input for a lost window is cancelled or marked "uncertain - review"
+  - a restarted simulator (new window handle) is only offered as a candidate; nothing is
+    controlled until it is registered again
+  - temporary capture failures and a minimised window back off and recover safely
+  - several tables: closing one stops only that one
+  - emergency stop wins over any recovery step
+  - a window whose identity no longer matches gets no input and inherits no permission
+  - scripted practice still plays hand after hand (no regression)
+Nothing needs to be installed: the bundled Node.js and the bundled programs are used.
+The EightMax 5.1 engine is only identified (SHA-256 and build id); it is not changed.
+
+BEFORE YOU START
+  1. Extract the complete ZIP into a NEW folder (do not copy over an older version).
+  2. Close the EightMax Workbench and its dashboard (the tests need port 48713).
+  3. Close or minimise other full-screen programs. Keep the computer awake.
+
+HOW TO RUN
+  Double-click   RUN-0362-MILESTONE2-TESTS.cmd
+  Press a key when asked. The test then runs by itself for about 10-15 minutes.
+  The mouse moves by itself inside small "EightMax Test Table" windows that open, close,
+  minimise, reopen and resize. Do NOT touch the mouse or keyboard until the window says
+  "MILESTONE 2 TESTS PASSED" or "FAILED" (touching the mouse makes the input driver yield,
+  which is reported as a failure). Ctrl+Alt+F12 still stops all input if you need it.
+
+WHERE THE RESULTS ARE SAVED
+  A results folder next to RUN-0362-MILESTONE2-TESTS.cmd:
+      test-results\Milestone2-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS\
+  and a ZIP of it:
+      test-results\Milestone2-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.zip      <- send this file back
+  (If the package folder is not writable, the folder is created under
+   %LOCALAPPDATA%\EightMax-Test-Workbench\Milestone2-0.36.2\ instead; the window shows the path.)
+  The folder opens in Explorer when the run ends.
+
+  Inside the folder:
+    milestone2-results.txt     plain summary: machine, every check, error / warning counts, OVERALL
+    milestone2-results.json    the same, machine-readable
+    lifecycle-acceptance.json  every real-window scenario (A-K) with each check and its measurements
+    unit-tests.tap             lifecycle unit / regression test output
+    *.out.txt / *.err.txt      raw logs
+
+WHAT THE RESULT MEANS
+  OVERALL: PASS   every required check passed on this computer.
+  OVERALL: FAIL   at least one check failed; the failing check names are listed in
+                  milestone2-results.txt. Send the ZIP; nothing on your computer was changed
+                  except the results folder.
+  Warnings (for example a leftover process) do not make the run fail but are listed.
+
+OPTIONS (advanced, from a command prompt in the package folder)
+  RUN-0362-MILESTONE2-TESTS.cmd -SkipAcceptance     identities and unit tests only (no windows, no mouse)
+  RUN-0362-MILESTONE2-TESTS.cmd -Only A,C,G         only the listed real-window scenarios
+
+Scenario letters: J scripted gameplay, A close during capture, B close during mouse movement,
+C restart with a new handle, D temporary capture failures, E minimised window, F several tables,
+G emergency stop during recovery, H repeated loss signals, I identity mismatch, K window resize.
