+## When a simulator window closes, minimises or restarts (0.36.2 Milestone 2)
+
+Every registered window has a **lifecycle state**, shown in the *Lifecycle* column of the table list:
+
+| State | Meaning | What happens | What you do |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| REGISTERED | Window registered, not verified yet | Nothing is sent until its identity and a first reading are verified | Start automation |
+| ACTIVE | Window exists, capture and reading work | Automation may act (when started) | — |
+| TEMPORARILY_UNAVAILABLE | Window exists but no usable frame (minimised, capture timeout, unreadable image) | No input; capture retries with growing pauses (0.25 s … 4 s), at most 5 minutes | Restore / uncover the window |
+| RECOVERY_PENDING | Capture works again | The window identity is checked again and fresh readings must agree before any input | Wait (a few seconds) |
+| TARGET_LOST | The window closed, or its handle now belongs to another program | Automation for this table stops for good: no capture, no input, pending input cancelled | Reopen the simulator, *Refresh registered windows*, review the replacement, register it |
+| STOPPED | You stopped automation | Nothing is sent | Start again (the window is verified again first) |
+| SAFETY_PAUSED | Emergency stop, manual mouse/keyboard input, an unconfirmed action, or capture unavailable for too long | Nothing is sent and nothing resumes by itself | Check the simulator, then *Resume* or Start |
+
+Messages you may see:
+
+* **Simulator window closed** — "The registered simulator is no longer available. Automation for this table has stopped. Reopen the simulator and register its window again."
+* **Capture temporarily unavailable** — "The simulator is still open, but the latest frame could not be captured. No actions will be sent until the current state is verified."
+* **Window identity changed** — "The selected window no longer matches the registered simulator. Automation has been disabled."
+
+**Replacing a closed simulator window.** Reopen the simulator and press **Refresh registered windows** (or **Review replacement window**). A window of the *same program* (same executable SHA-256) is offered under *Replacement window review* with a side-by-side comparison (handle, process, size, display scaling). It is **not controlled** until you tick the three confirmations and press *Register this window as the replacement*; the registration gets a fresh authorisation and its calibration is checked against the new window. If the window size or display scaling changed, run *Preview mouse movement* first. Automation for the replacement stays **off** until you press *Enable automation for this table* (while automation runs) or *Start*. **Remove lost registration** deletes a lost entry. While the emergency stop is latched, no replacement can be registered.
+
+An action that was already on its way when the window closed is marked **uncertain (REVIEW)** in the *Confirmation* column; it is never repeated. **Export diagnostic report** writes the lifecycle history of every registration (including replaced ones), the cancelled work and separate counts for capture failures, recognition failures, strategy unavailable, input cancellations, emergency stops, manual overrides and lost windows. Repeated identical failures appear once with a repeat count.
+
